Table full name: bigquery-public-data.utility_us.us_cities_area
Column name: urban_area_code Type: STRING Description: Urban area code from the 2010 Census
Column name: geo_code Type: STRING Description: Unique identifier for each urban area; Same as urban_area_code
Column name: name Type: STRING Description: Full text name for the urban area
Column name: lsad_name Type: STRING Description: 2010 Census name and the translated legal/statistical area description of a given urban area
Column name: lsad_code Type: STRING Description: Legal/Statistical area description (LSAD) code for a given urban area. 

75 indicates an "urbanized area"
76 indicates an "urban cluster"
Column name: feature_class_code Type: STRING Description: 5-digit code assigned by the Census Bureau intended to classify and describe geographic objects or features. 
"G3500" indicates "urban area"
Column name: area_type Type: STRING Description: 2010 Census urban area type. 

C indicates an "urban cluster", which is an area with a population between 2,500 and 49,999 
U indicates an "urbanized area", which is an area with a population greater than or equal to 50,000

More information on how the Census Bureau made these determinations can be found here: https://www.census.gov/geo/reference/urban-rural.html
Column name: functional_status Type: STRING Description: Current functional status code. A full list of possible results can be found: https://www.census.gov/geo/reference/funcstat.html 
"A" refers to "active government providing primary general-purpose functions"
